# {{SYSTEM_NAME}}

`{{PACKAGE_NAME}}` is a portable React design system implementing the canonical
V2 contract. It is intentionally a small, readable starting point for the
Design Brief below rather than a finished product language.

## Design brief

- Summary: {{BRIEF_SUMMARY}}
- Visual direction: {{VISUAL_DIRECTION}}
- Avoid: {{AVOID_LIST}}

## Installation

```bash
pnpm add {{PACKAGE_NAME}}
```

The package is built for React 18+ and depends on `@prism-system/ui-core`.

## Setup

Import the stylesheet once, before any components render:

```tsx
import "{{PACKAGE_NAME}}/styles.css";
```

## Usage

```tsx
import { Button, Card } from "{{PACKAGE_NAME}}";
import "{{PACKAGE_NAME}}/styles.css";

export function Example() {
  return (
    <Card>
      <Card.Header>
        <Card.Title>Continue</Card.Title>
      </Card.Header>
      <Card.Content>
        <Button>Continue</Button>
      </Card.Content>
    </Card>
  );
}
```

## Package API

The package root exports the fourteen V2 components together with their compound
static members (for example `Card.Header`, `Tabs.List`, `Select.Item`,
`Dialog.Content`). Design tokens are available from `{{PACKAGE_NAME}}/tokens`.

### Components

Every V2 design system provides the same component set:

- `Button`
- `Input`
- `Textarea`
- `Card`
- `Badge`
- `Checkbox`
- `RadioGroup`
- `Switch`
- `Select`
- `Tabs`
- `Dialog`
- `DropdownMenu`
- `Tooltip`
- `Separator`

Components use only `@prism-system/ui-core` for behavior and React; this package
owns the visual tokens, CSS, and component composition.

## Development

```bash
pnpm build
pnpm typecheck
pnpm lint
```

Refine `src/tokens`, `src/styles`, and `src/components` together. Keep the
system class on every visual component so the package can be safely consumed
alongside another design system.

## Manifest and version

Every installed package ships a generated `design-system.json` manifest,
available at `{{PACKAGE_NAME}}/manifest`. It records the exact package version,
the component catalog, variants, sizes, compound members, and the strict usage
rules for this system. `package.json.version` is authoritative, and the manifest,
the registry entry, and the runtime `DesignSystem.version` must always match it.
Regenerate the manifest with `pnpm ds:manifest {{SYSTEM_ID}} --write` after
changing the package-owned `design-system.source.json`. After `changeset version`
changes `package.json.version`, run `pnpm ds:sync-versions` from the monorepo
root to align the runtime version, the generated manifest, and the registry
entry; `pnpm ds:sync-versions --check` fails without writing when they drift.

## Consumer contract

- **Identity:** the visual source of truth is `{{PACKAGE_NAME}}` at the installed
  version.
- **Available UI:** the fourteen V2 components above, their compound members, and
  the tokens from `{{PACKAGE_NAME}}/tokens`.
- **Usage rules:** prefer existing components, use props rather than class
  overrides, and keep layout in the product while the visual language stays here.
- **Restrictions:** no arbitrary colors, radius, or shadows; no duplicated
  primitives; no local replacements for components that already exist here.
- **Extension:** reusable visual patterns belong in the design system; product
  and feature components stay in the product and are composed from these
  primitives.
